		<item>
		<title>OpenAI is steering ChatGPT users toward more paid usage</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/openai-is-steering-chatgpt-users-toward-more-paid-usage/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/openai-is-steering-chatgpt-users-toward-more-paid-usage/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Matthias Bastian]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 12:05:04 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Short News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ChatGPT]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[OpenAI]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42269</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/openai_chatgpt.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI is now capping the number of paid ChatGPT accounts per device and payment card. Users who hit the limit can't start new subscriptions, and affected accounts can't be used on that device. Logging out doesn't automatically free up a spot. The policy will likely hit users who've been juggling multiple cheap subscriptions to maximize usage, pushing them toward pricier options like buying extra credits.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/openai-is-steering-chatgpt-users-toward-more-paid-usage/">OpenAI is steering ChatGPT users toward more paid usage</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
